I don't want you to slip either, so let me put a price on it instead of just saying no.

If v2 misbehaves and we have never rolled it back, the rollback is the untested part - that is where the hours go. On a Friday evening those hours land on whoever is on call over the weekend, and the carriers it was promised to absorb the failed routes Saturday morning. A rehearsed rollback is ten minutes; an unrehearsed one, in my experience, is an evening.

Two ways to keep the date: (1) ship Friday at 5% of traffic behind the flag, so a bad rollback hurts 5% of routes and we rehearse for real in production; or (2) keep 100% but move it to Tuesday, when the whole team is around. Either keeps the promise to the carriers - their kickoff is the 22nd. What I would not do is 100% on a Friday with a rollback nobody has run.

Morgan

